{"kind":"request","text":"Deliver the head-notice bell, and stop one cold audit from stalling the whole resident.","body":{"conditions":"The kernel contract names watch — per-log head notices — as its minimal bell; nothing implements it, so every waiting client drives a 250ms poll that spawns a git rev-parse subprocess four times a second per waiter, and wait replays the full snapshot rather than a delta. Separately, Workspace.Snapshot holds its mutex across an entire cold load, so one cold audit stalls every status, wait, and act on the resident for its full duration — at current depth that is tens of seconds. Give the resident a single shared head-change notifier that waiters block on instead of individual polls; make cold loads single-flight without holding the snapshot lock against readers of the previous snapshot; measure subprocess count and wait latency before and after at scaled depth. This composes with, and does not replace, the bounded status and wait shapes of the efficient-status task. Obtain independent exact-head review before merge.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}